            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0315" n="288" xml:id="pg288"/>

                <head>137. Memorandum From the Assistant Secretary of State for Far Eastern Affairs
                    (Hilsman) to the Deputy Director of the Office of Southeast Asian Affairs
                        (Hannah)<anchor n="0" xml:id="d137-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1963-12-16">December 16,
                        1963</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Cambodia</item>
                </list>
                <p>In a conversation between Acheson, Harriman, Hilsman and Forrestal today, it was
                    agreed that, to provide a basis for considering whether or not Acheson should
                    make a trip to Cambodia, we would draft a treaty on Cambodia’s neutrality,
                    including an enlarged ICC along the lines Sihanouk desires, which we would be
                    content to sign if it could be negotiated without a conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">RH</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
